# Kid Loki's hexproof reaches "each creature you control that you've put one or more +1/+1 counters on this turn", not only
# itself. In turn 3 Bot1 casts A.I.M. Scientists (Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire), which connives: Bot1 draws a Lightning Bolt,
# the second card of the turn (Kid Loki grows too), and discards it, so the Scientists get a counter. Both have hexproof at the
# end step: Bot2's Bolt cannot target the Scientists (the refusal). A creature Bot1 has put no counter on, the Ornithopter
# cast in turn 1, is not hexproof.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Kid Loki
A.I.M. Scientists
Ornithopter
Island x2
Lightning Bolt
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kid Loki.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.A.I.M. Scientists.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Battlefield.A.I.M. Scientists.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.A.I.M. Scientists.Keywords = Hexproof
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kid Loki.Keywords = Hexproof
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.A.I.M. Scientists)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)
